## Summary

- make `FusedSequence` a public immutable dense-output contract with defensive copying, canonical dtypes, and read-only arrays;
- fail closed on non-finite, asymmetric, or materially indefinite active point/flow covariance;
- validate dense `3 x 3` covariance in bounded chunks, using a principal-minor fast path and the existing scale-aware eigensolver only for numerically suspicious matrices;
- let fusion and fused-artifact loading transfer privately owned arrays into the same contract without a second dense copy;
- add adversarial immutability, covariance-admission, fast-path, and artifact-load regressions;
- document the compatibility boundary and refresh the complete Unreleased changelog.

## Root cause

`@dataclass(frozen=True)` protected attribute assignment but did not freeze the referenced NumPy buffers. The previous `__post_init__` converted arrays only into local validation variables, so caller-owned arrays could still mutate a validated sequence and the apparent dtype normalization was not retained. Active covariance validity was also deferred to later consumers.

